{
  "id": "object-based-attention",
  "term": "object-based attention",
  "definition": "Object-based attention is attention guided by perceived objects or grouped events rather than by isolated sensory parts. In this study, when speech sounds were heard as whole word-like auditory objects, that grouping made it harder to focus on and discriminate changes in one component unless the sounds were reorganized into separate attended and ignored objects.",
