      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s contrast—“rather than by isolated sensory parts”—is not stated in the packet. The packet describes object-based grouping and attentional reorganization affecting discrimination, but it does not explicitly claim that attention is “guided … rather than” by isolated sensory parts.",
        "The phrase “whole word-like auditory objects” is not used in the packet; the packet describes CvC words being perceived in terms of auditory objects that group bursts and vowels. While conceptually related, the specific wording/“word-like” characterization is not directly supported."
